      "name": "What's the most common tree in NE Ohio yards?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Maple — both red maple and sugar maple — is the most common large tree in established NE Ohio yards, followed by oak (mixed species), American beech, ash (declining due to EAB), and white pine. Mature suburban canopy in the inner-ring villages of Greater Cleveland is dominated by oaks and maples that were planted 60–100+ years ago." }
