      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can I tell what kind of tree I have?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Three quick checks: leaf shape (lobed, simple, compound, needle-like), bark pattern (smooth, furrowed, peeling, scaly), and branching habit (opposite vs alternate). Opposite branching is rare and points to maple, ash, dogwood, or horsechestnut; everything else is alternate. If you're stuck, photograph the leaf, bark, and overall form and call {{global.phone}} — we can usually ID a tree from a phone photo." }
    },
