      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is my ash tree definitely going to die from EAB?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Most untreated mature ash in NE Ohio that haven't already died eventually will. The regional emerald ash borer outbreak began in 2008 and has now killed an estimated 90%+ of ash trees in Cuyahoga and Geauga counties. Smaller, otherwise-healthy ash can sometimes be preserved with annual emamectin benzoate trunk injections, but treatment must begin before significant damage and is most cost-effective on smaller trees. Plan removal for any ash showing D-shaped exit holes and crown dieback." }
    },
