      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What tree should I plant to replace a dead ash?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "It depends on the spot. For a similar-sized canopy tree, sugar maple, white oak, bur oak, or American beech are excellent long-term choices. For faster establishment, tulip poplar or red maple. Avoid replanting another ash — the EAB pressure isn't going away. The recommended-plantings table above lists the best 2026 choices." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why does Roubic refuse to prune oak trees in summer?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Oak wilt is a fungal disease vectored by sap-feeding nitidulid beetles, and the high-risk window in Ohio runs roughly April 1 through July 31. Pruning during that window creates fresh wounds the beetles are attracted to, and a single infected cut can introduce oak wilt that kills the tree within two seasons and spreads to adjacent oaks through root grafts. We won't prune your oak in May or June regardless of urgency." }
